WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.840
When you send on Aztec,

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.080
the private part of the work

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:04.800
happens on your computer,

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.360
not on the network.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.240
Nulo runs it right here,

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.600
with your keys and your notes.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.120
Your keys, and what is in your notes,

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.280
stay on your computer.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.680
Then your computer builds a proof:

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.480
math that shows this private

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:20.880
part follows the rules,

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.880
without showing what is in it.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.680
The proof goes to the network,

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.147
with sealed notes for the people you pay.

00:00:27.147 --> 00:00:28.800
The network checks the proof,

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.040
and if it holds, the transaction

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.440
joins a block.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.000
It never needed your private

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.280
data to trust it.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.760
Anything a transaction does in public,

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.520
the network runs in the open,

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.200
for everyone to see.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.600
Later, one proof for a whole batch

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.920
of blocks is checked on Ethereum.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.160
Building a proof takes real work,

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.720
so it is the slow step before sending.
